  "strategy": "1. **Approach and rationale**\n\nWe propose using Evolutionary Strategies (ES) combined with gradient-based refinement to address the Erd\u0151s minimum overlap problem. ES is chosen for its ability to efficiently explore the solution space through mutation and selection, particularly suited for non-convex optimization. Unlike PSO or SA, ES maintains a population of candidate solutions, promoting diversity and reducing the risk of premature convergence. The key bottlenecks addressed are premature convergence and local optima trapping.\n\n2. **Mathematical specification**\n\n- Representation: h is an array of size n_points, with h[i] \u2208 [0,1] and \u2211h[i] = n_points/2.\n\n- Objective: Minimize C\u2085 = max_k (correlate(h, 1\u2212h, mode=\"full\") * dx).\n\n- Constraints:\n  - 0 \u2264 h[i] \u2264 1\n  - \u2211h[i] = n_points/2\n\n- Mutation: Gaussian noise with varying step sizes.\n\n- Selection: Truncation selection based on C\u2085 scores.\n\n3. **Implementation procedure**\n\n**a. Initialization**\n- Use initial_h_values if available; else, create balanced step function.\n\n**b. ES Setup**\n- Population size: 50-100\n- Mutation step size: Initial \u03c3=0.1, adaptive adjustment\n- Number of iterations: 1000\n- Elitism rate: 20%\n\n**c. ES Loop**\n1. Generate offspring via Gaussian mutation\n2. Repair solutions to meet constraints\n3. Evaluate C\u2085 for each candidate\n4. Select top candidates for next generation\n\n**d. Mutation details**\n- For each candidate, add Gaussian noise \u223cN(0, \u03c3\u00b2) to 30-50% of elements\n- Clip to [0,1], rescale to maintain sum constraint\n\n**e. Termination**\n- Stop when time budget exhausted or C\u2085 < 0.3807\n\n**f. SLSQP Refinement**\n- Apply gradient descent to best ES solution\n\n4. **Search choices and useful variations**\n\n- Population size: 100\n- Mutation step size: \u03c3=0.1, adaptive based on improvement\n- Elitism rate: 20%\n- Mutation strength adaptation: increase \u03c3 if no improvement, reset if improvement\n\n5. **Compute budget and robustness**\n\n- ES iterations: 90% budget\n- SLSQP refinement: 10% budget\n- Periodic checkpointing\n- Mutation strength adaption rules\n\n6. **Validation and return contract**\n\n- Re-evaluate constraints\n- Compute C\u2085 using evaluator\n- Fallback to initial_h_values if needed",
